    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41011": {
      "title": "Temporary Mobile Program Coordinator",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary Mobile Program Coordinator - Clinical Support (Part-time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary Mobile Program Coordinator - Clinical Support (Part-time) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N. C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance from their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this role is to support the School of Nursing in coordinating and delivering mobile-based simulation experiences and community wellness events. This part-time position is ideal for a Licensed Practical Nurse ( LPN ) or Registered Nurse (RN) who is passionate about hands-on education, preventive health, and community engagement. The Coordinator will provide clinical and logistical support, help with event setup and simulation activities, and drive the mobile unit when necessary. Work Hours: 10-20 hours per week, with flexible scheduling based on events (includes occasional evenings or weekends) Primary Function of Organizational Unit The School of Nursing is dedicated to equipping individuals for the nursing profession, ensuring they possess the essential skills & knowledge for quality, safe, patient-centered care. Our comprehensive program offerings include traditional bachelor of science in nursing ( BSN ) tracks, Accelerated Bachelor of Science in Nursing ( ABSN ), and RN to BSN pathways. We are proud to offer a new Doctor of Nursing program, further expanding our educational horizons. Students in all programs benefit from academic excellence fostered in small, flexible classes guided by supportive faculty. Minimum Requirements Applicant must hold a current & unrestricted RN license in North Carolina or Compact State License Minimum of two years of clinical experience (community health, simulation, or education experience preferred) Valid driver’s license with willingness to drive the mobile unit (training provided) Strong organizational & interpersonal communication skills. Comfortable working with diverse populations & learners in both clinical & community settings. Able to lift up to 30lbs & assist with equipment setup & take down BLS Certification (required or must be obtained within 60 days of hire) Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Experience with health fairs, wellness outreach, or nursing education. Familiarity with simulation-based learning tools & mannequins (preferred but not required). Flexible, team-oriented, and committed to health equity and access Required License or Certification RN or LPN License Driver’s License BLS Certification (required or must be obtained within 60 days of hire) Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Position Information Working Title Temporary Mobile Program Coordinator - Clinical Support (Part-time) Position Number Recruitment Salary Range $33 per hour FLSA Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Part-time Tenure Track No FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division School of Nursing Organizational Location College of Health and Human Sciences Organizational Unit School of Nursing Posting Detail Information Posting Number EPA3116 Open Date 07/16/2026 Close Date - for postings that do not use Open Until Filled Open Until Filled Yes Open Until Filled Minimum Application Period Postings: Positions remaining posted after this date are continuing to accept applications, but may close at any time. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration, applications received after this date may receive consideration depending upon the status of the search 07/30/2026 Date Position Available As soon as possible Special Instructions to Applicant You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N. C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance from their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/40750 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this employment opportunity: North Carolina A&T State University employment web page University of North Carolina System employment web page Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Education Research Consortium (HERC) Indeed.com Listserv Other * If you indicated you learned of this employment opportunity from an “Other” source please advise where you learned of the position: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Cover Letter Other Document Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
