    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/40459": {
      "title": "Director of Finance",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Director of Finance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Director of Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more: Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex - Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System (TSERS) Optional Supplemental Plans - 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type EHRA Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position Reporting to the Executive Director for Administration, the Director of Finance serves as the department’s senior liaison to the division regarding student affairs business operations. The Director of Finance serves as a member of the Office of the Vice Chancellor for Student Affairs team and supports the Executive Director for Administration in the coordinating the administrative operations for the Division of Student Affairs, comprised of a community of approximately 500 professional and student employees who steward fiscal resources of $90 million and approximately 1,000,000 square feet in facilities to support student success. The Director will serve as a deputy to the Executive Director for Administration and will serve the division in their absence. Primary Function of Organizational Unit The Director of Finance is a critical position within the Division of Student Affairs, responsible for the comprehensive management of all financial activities that directly support the division’s mission and strategic objectives. This role ensures the integrity and accuracy of financial transactions, budget planning, and fiscal reporting, providing essential oversight that safeguards the division’s resources and promotes operational efficiency. By maintaining rigorous compliance with university policies and regulatory requirements, the Director of Finance mitigates financial risk and supports informed decision-making at all levels. The position’s expertise in financial analysis and process improvement is vital for sustaining high-quality services and programs that enrich student life and advance institutional goals. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s Degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, or related business area or equivalent combination of training and experience. Minimum of five years demonstrated success leading and organizing complex and confidential budget actions in a higher education administrative setting. Strong proficiency in university budgeting processes, policies and technological solutions. Experience managing multiple priorities and stakeholders in a culturally diverse environment. Strong knowledge of higher education administrative operations. Excellent writing, organizational, and communication skills. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Master’s degree in Business Administration, Finance or related field. Seven years of experience leading and organizing complex and confidential budget actions in a higher education administrative setting. Intermediate Proficiency with Banner 9, Aggie Mart (Jaggaer), and Emburse Enterprise (Chrome River). Strong capabilities and experience in managing cross-functional projects. Understanding of a midsize, doctoral, land-grant, research university. Demonstrated ability to successfully lead, develop and manage professional staff. Prior experience processing and managing internal and external financial resources (e.g., state, non-state, gifts, federal grants, etc.) Required License or Certification Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. On-site (Employees are primarily in the office and/or have a critical job requirement that requires dedicated office space on-site) Position Information Working Title Director of Finance Position Number 000456 Recruitment Salary Range Commensurate with education and experience FLSA Exempt Appointment Type Permanent - Full-time Tenure Track No FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Administration Organizational Location VC for Student Affairs Organizational Unit VC for Student Affairs Posting Detail Information Posting Number EPA2994 Open Date 02/23/2026 Close Date - for postings that do not use Open Until Filled Open Until Filled Yes Open Until Filled Minimum Application Period Postings: Positions remaining posted after this date are continuing to accept applications, but may close at any time. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration, applications received after this date may receive consideration depending upon the status of the search Date Position Available Immediately Special Instructions to Applicant You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more: Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex – Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System ( TSERS ) Optional Supplemental Plans – 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/39699 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have experience with the Ellucian/Banner system? If yes, please indicate the module(s) for which you have experience Yes No * Have you worked within the University of North Carolina (UNC) System. If yes, please describe the institution, your role, and the nature of your experience? (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your management experience, including the size of teams you have supervised, areas of oversight, and your approach to leadership and team development. (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate where you learned of this position: North Carolina A&T State University website University of North Carolina System website Chronicle of Higher Education InsideHigherEd.com Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) Indeed.com Other If you indicated you learned of this employment opportunity from an “Other” source please advise where you learned of the position: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Bachelor's Degree - Copy of transcripts Master's Degree -  Copy of transcripts Other Degree - Copy of transcripts Terminal Degree - Copy of transcripts Statement of Leadership and Management Philosophy Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
