      "title": "Temporary Part-Time Associate Director",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary Part-Time Associate Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary Part-Time Associate Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position This is a temporary, part-time position with administrative responsibilities and reports to the Program Director. The part-time associate director within the Physician Assistant (PA) Program is primarily responsible for curriculum development, instruction, and/or course coordination in the didactic and/or clinical phase of the program. It is expected that the associate director will be effective in the areas of course design, course delivery, and evaluation. The associate director is instrumental in ensuring the program is meeting the Accreditation Review Commission on Education for Physician Assistant ( ARC -PA) Accreditation Standards. Work Hours: Hours vary Monday – Friday 8:00 a.m. – 6:00 p.m.) ***No more than 20 hours per week Primary Function of Organizational Unit To prepare highly qualified, diverse graduates to provide comprehensive, patient-centered care, particularly for underserved communities in North Carolina. The 27-month, full-time, Master’s-level program aims to address regional provider shortages by training practitioners in both didactic and clinical settings. Minimum Requirements Masters degree – Physician Assistant Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Doctorate degree – Physician Assistant Required License or Certification N/A Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Position Information Working Title Temporary Part-Time Associate Director Position Number Recruitment Salary Range $60 per hour FLSA Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Part-time Tenure Track No FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Physician Assistant Program Organizational Location College of Health and Human Sciences Organizational Unit Physician Assistant Program Posting Detail Information Posting Number EPA2990 Open Date 02/13/2026 Close Date - for postings