      "title": "Temporary IT Support Specialist",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary IT Support Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary IT Support Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title Classification Type Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: Minimum Experience/Education Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Minimum: Associates degree in a relevant field of study or a combination of education and experience Basic computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, Outlook). Preferred: Bachelor’s degree in computer science, Information Technology, or related discipline Two years of relative experience. Required License or Certification N/A Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position Position Purpose North Carolina A&T State University periodically has temporary staffing needs within the field of Information Technology (IT). This recruitment is intended to identify qualified candidates for temporary IT opportunities as workforce needs arise across the University. Temporary assignments may be available at various levels and across a broad range of IT disciplines, including technical support, systems administration, application support, cybersecurity, network services, web development, and other technology-related functions. Assignment length, work schedule, and level of responsibility will vary based on departmental needs. Potential Duties and Responsibilities Duties may include, but are not limited to: Desktop and end-user device support Software installation, configuration, and updates System monitoring, maintenance, and troubleshooting Technology-related communications and information support Website maintenance and development Enterprise-level IT support and services Other duties as assigned by the supervisor Additional Information Specific job duties, qualifications, work schedules, and assignment durations will vary depending on the needs of the hiring department and the nature of the temporary assignment. Details regarding the position will be discussed with candidates selected for an interview. Only applicants who meet the minimum qualifications for a temporary opportunity will be considered. To enhance consideration, applicants are encouraged to upload all relevant certifications, licenses, training records, and other professional credentials at the time of application. Please Note: This posting will remain active for six (6) months. Applicants who wish to be considered for temporary opportunities after the posting has expired must submit a new application to the subsequent posting. Primary Function of Organizational Unit Information Technology Services ( ITS ) is responsible for strengthening and supporting the University’s learning, discovery, and engagement activities by providing the information technology infrastructure, software, hardware and support to position the University on a path of operational excellence that integrates advanced technologies to enhance teaching, learning and research. ITS is comprised of seven operating units that report to the Office of the Vice Chancellor/ CIO . These operating units are: Enterprise IT Support Services, IT Security Services, Enterprise Applications Services, Infrastructure Services, Learning Technology Services, IT Operations Services and the Project Management Office. These units work collaboratively and cooperatively within the organization and across the university community to provide the information technology support and services required for the University. Work Hours 8:00am - 5:00pm; Monday - Friday; hours may vary Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Position Information Working Title Temporary IT Support Specialist Competency Level Contributing Position Number Recruitment Range Commensurate with experience FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Full-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Client Technology Services Organizational Location VC for Info Tech Services Organizational Unit Client Technology Services Posting Detail Information Posting Number SHRA3262 Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Special Instructions to Applicant To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41533 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this employment opportunity: North Carolina A&T State University employment web page University of North Carolina System employment web page Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Education Research Consortium (HERC) Indeed.com Listserv Other * Please indicate any certifications you possess such as A+, Network+, etc. (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate your years of experience as a help desk technician/technology support technician. Less than 1 year 1 - 2 years 2 - 3 years 3 years or more * Please describe your proficiencies with various computer technology systems and software programs such as Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Banner, AggieMart, and any other technology systems. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Cover Letter Other Document Other Degree - Copy of transcripts Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
