    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41683": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Program Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Program Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more; Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex - Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System (TSERS) Optional Supplemental Plans - 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title University Program Specialist Classification Type SHRA Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: N - Not Mandatory Minimum Experience/Education Bachelor’s degree and one year of experience related to the area of assignment; or and equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Master’s Degree from a four-year college or university in education, humanities, student affairs, social work, sociology or related field. Two years of professional’s experience as program coordinator in a student services area or in related field. Successful implementation of programs for different student population, and evidence of successful college-wide collaborations. Required License or Certification Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The Program Coordinator will provide management for the day-to-day programming activities and will serve as the primary administrative point of contact for the program. The Program Coordinator will work with Center of Excellence for Social Justice’ ( CESJ ) students, partners, staff, and other university constituents. The position will be responsible for fostering a sense of pride and support for the Center, and for helping the CESJ achieve its mission and goals. Primary Function of Organizational Unit The Center of Excellence for Social Justice draws upon the interdisciplinary academic and historical resources of North Carolina A&T State University to support in-depth academic examination of topics such as race, economics, higher education, civil rights, public policy and related areas of study. Through research and academic inquiry, the center examines how these subjects have shaped the development of the United States and continue to influence contemporary society. The Center manages The Power of Four Fellowship Program, which focuses on selecting four freshman students each year, providing them with the resources and support to scale up national and global social equality projects during their four years at A&T; the Social Justice Scholar-in-Residence program, which will bring exemplary activists who champion issues on campus; and the Youth in Action Prize, which will exemplify the legacy and tradition of activism among young people. Additionally, the center provides Building Bridges Roundtable, which will provide local community members with the opportunity to create a stronger opportunity by gathering university student, faculty and staff. Host an annual Truth and Transformation Conference. Work Hours M-F 8-5pm Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. On-site (Employees are primarily in the office and/or have a critical job requirement that requires dedicated office space on-site) Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Required Competency Information Analysis and Decision Making Duties Collect, analyze, and interpret program participation data, assessment results, and stakeholder feedback to evaluate program effectiveness. Prepare reports and presentations summarizing outcomes, performance metrics, and recommendations for program enhancements. Monitor compliance with university policies, grant guidelines, and reporting requirements. Use data-informed decision-making to identify trends, recommend improvements, and support strategic planning efforts for CESJ initiatives. Required Competency Communication and Marketing Duties Develop and implement communication strategies to increase awareness of CESJ programs, research initiatives, events, and community engagement opportunities. Create and distribute promotional materials, social media content, newsletters, website updates, and event announcements for internal and external audiences. Serve as a liaison between CESJ , university departments, students, faculty, community organizations, and external partners to support collaboration and engagement. Coordinate outreach efforts that advance the Center’s mission of promoting social justice education, research, and community impact. Required Competency Program/Project Administration Duties Coordinate, implement, and evaluate CESJ programs, initiatives, conferences, workshops, community engagement projects, and special events. Develop project timelines, monitor program objectives, and ensure deliverables are completed in accordance with institutional and grant requirements. Manage event logistics, scheduling, participant registration, travel arrangements, and communications with faculty, students, community partners, and external stakeholders. Maintain program records, budgets, reports, and assessment data to support operational effectiveness and continuous improvement. Position Information Working Title Program Coordinator Competency Level Journey Position Number 007840 Recruitment Range $51,285 - $55,000 FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Time Limited - Full-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length 03/31/2027 Organizational Division College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences Organizational Location College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences Organizational Unit College of Arts, Humanities, and Social Sciences Posting Detail Information Posting Number SHRA3267 Open Date 09/25/2026 Close Date 10/02/2026 Special Instructions to Applicant You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more; Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex – Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System ( TSERS ) Optional Supplemental Plans – 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41582 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Bachelor's Degree - Copy of transcripts Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
