    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41538": {
      "title": "Temporary Ticketing & Event Services Associate",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary Ticketing &amp; Event Services Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary Ticketing & Event Services Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title Classification Type Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: Minimum Experience/Education Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Minimum Requirement HS Diploma, equivalency or combination of education and experience One year of customer service experience Basic computer skills, including proficiency in MS office applications (Word, Excel, Outlook, etc.) Preferred Requirement Experience with POS transactions and computer applications Experience supporting event management & services Required License or Certification Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position Position Purpose North Carolina A&T State University periodically has temporary part-time staffing needs to support operations within the Ticketing Office and at athletic and university-sponsored events. This recruitment is intended to identify qualified candidates for temporary event and ticketing opportunities as workforce needs arise. Temporary assignments may be available in a variety of event support functions, including ticket sales, customer service, concessions, event operations, and facility support. Assignments may support athletic competitions, commencement ceremonies, concerts, conferences, and other university-sponsored events. Assignment length, work schedule, and level of responsibility will vary based on departmental needs, with many positions requiring evening, weekend, and holiday availability. Potential Duties and Responsibilities Duties may include, but are not limited to: Selling and distributing event tickets in person, online, or by phone Providing excellent customer service to patrons, guests, and event attendees Assisting with ticket scanning, admissions, and guest entry procedures Responding to questions regarding event schedules, seating, policies, and venue information Supporting concession operations, including food and beverage sales Assisting with event setup, breakdown, and venue preparation activities Performing environmental services functions to help maintain a clean, safe, and welcoming facility Monitoring assigned areas to support positive guest experiences and venue operations Assisting with crowd management and directing patrons to designated locations Operating point-of-sale systems, cash handling equipment, and related event technology Providing general administrative and operational support as needed Performing other duties as assigned by the supervisor Additional Information Specific job duties, qualifications, work schedules, and assignment durations will vary depending on the needs of the hiring department and the nature of the temporary assignment. Details regarding individual opportunities will be discussed with candidates selected for an interview. Only applicants who meet the minimum qualifications for a temporary opportunity will be considered. To enhance consideration, applicants are encouraged to upload all relevant certifications, licenses, training records, and other professional credentials at the time of application. Please Note: This posting will remain active for six (6) months. Applicants who wish to be considered for temporary opportunities after the posting has expired must submit a new application to the subsequent posting. Primary Function of Organizational Unit The mission of the Ticket Office is to support the University community and external guests by managing, promoting, and facilitating ticket sales for Athletics and other university-sponsored events. The Ticket Office is committed to delivering exceptional customer service and creating a positive experience for patrons attending events at North Carolina A&T State University. North Carolina A&T State University sponsors 13 varsity athletic programs and competes at the NCAA Division I level. The University is a member of the Colonial Athletic Association ( CAA ) in all sports except Football and Women’s Bowling. Through its ticketing and event operations, the Ticket Office plays a vital role in supporting student-athletes, enhancing fan engagement, and contributing to the success of athletic competitions and campus events. The Ticket Office serves as a primary point of contact for event attendees, providing ticketing services, event information, and customer support while helping to foster an enjoyable and welcoming environment for all guests. Work Hours As needed basis; usually weekend or evening hours. Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Position Information Working Title Temporary Ticketing & Event Services Associate Competency Level Contributing Position Number Recruitment Range Commensurate with experience FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Part-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Staffing Services Organizational Location Human Resources Organizational Unit Temporary Employment Posting Detail Information Posting Number SHRA3263 Open Date 09/10/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Special Instructions to Applicant To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41535 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this employment opportunity: North Carolina A&T State University employment web page University of North Carolina System employment web page Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Education Research Consortium (HERC) Indeed.com Listserv Other * How many years of relevant point of sale or event services experience do you have? 1-2 years of experience 3-5 years of experiecne More than 5 years of experience Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Cover Letter Other Document Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
