    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41478": {
      "title": "Legal Operations Manager",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Legal Operations Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Legal Operations Manager Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more; Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex - Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System (TSERS) Optional Supplemental Plans - 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Classification Type EHRA Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to serve as a senior legal paraprofessional and business operations lead for the Division of Legal Affairs, Risk and Compliance ( DLARC ), performing substantive legal support work for the Office of Legal Affairs ( OLA ) while administering the division’s records, financial, and operational functions and providing executive-level support to the Vice Chancellor for Legal Affairs, Risk and Compliance and General Counsel. The position performs legal paraprofessional work of substantial complexity under the general direction of the General Counsel or designee. This includes conducting independent legal and factual research and analysis; drafting substantive legal documents, correspondence, and memoranda; assisting in the preparation and management of actual and potential litigation; administering the division’s contract intake, review tracking, and execution processes; and coordinating with outside counsel and the North Carolina Attorney General’s Office on matters handled on behalf of the University. Work requires independent judgment in the identification of legal issues, the organization of case and matter files, and the escalation of time-sensitive or high-exposure matters to the appropriate attorney. The position serves as the University’s primary public records officer, with responsibility for the intake, tracking, and fulfillment of public records requests in compliance with Chapter 132 of the North Carolina General Statutes. This includes coordinating record searches across University units, conducting privilege and confidentiality review, applying statutory exemptions and preparing redactions in consultation with OLA attorneys, monitoring statutory and internal response deadlines, and maintaining the division’s records in accordance with the applicable State retention and disposition schedules. The position further administers litigation holds and maintains confidential legal and investigative files, ensuring the accuracy, security, and defensibility of the division’s records. The position administers the financial and business operations of the division, including preparing and monitoring divisional budgets across multiple funding sources, reconciling expenditures, processing purchases and travel, and administering lease and vendor agreements in coordination with the Office of Budget and Planning and other campus units. The position compiles budget reports and analyses, monitors expenditures against divisional objectives, and identifies variances and compliance concerns for the Vice Chancellor’s attention. The position also provides executive support to the Vice Chancellor, managing a complex calendar, coordinating high-level meetings and special events, arranging travel, preparing agendas and briefing materials, and drafting correspondence with a high degree of independence and discretion. The position serves as administrative support to the N.C. A&T Board of Trustees’ Risk Management and Audit Committee, coordinates divisional human resources actions on behalf of the Vice Chancellor, and serves as the division’s Emergency Action Plan Coordinator and SECC representative. Given the nature of the work, the position requires exceptional judgment, discretion, and attention to detail, and the ability to manage concurrent legal, records, and financial matters under statutory and court-imposed deadlines in a high-volume, high-visibility environment. This position is essential to the division’s legal service delivery, its statutory records compliance posture, and its operational continuity. Primary Function of Organizational Unit The Division of Legal Affairs, Risk, and Compliance supports North Carolina A&T’s academic mission and strategic plan by working collaboratively with institutional and external partners to ensure an understanding of and adherence to the university’s ethical, legal, and regulatory responsibilities. The Division of Legal Affairs, Risk and Compliance ( DLARC ) consists of the Office of Legal Affairs ( OLA ), the Office of Compliance and Enterprise Risk Management, and the Title IX Office OLA provides comprehensive legal advice and assistance to the N.C. A&T Board of Trustees, the Chancellor, the other senior administrators of the University, and through them, the University’s faculty and staff, only on legal matters involving or affecting the institution. OLA advises the University on the legal implications of proposed policies and actions and on compliance with state and federal laws, regulations, and UNC policies. OLA drafts and reviews University contracts and other legal documents and is also available to provide educational services, including training programs on legal and policy matters, for any University constituency. OLA is responsible for selecting, engaging, and supervising any outside counsel engaged by the institution and coordinates all litigation conducted by the North Carolina Attorney General’s Office on behalf of the University. No attorneys other than those in the Office of Legal Affairs, outside counsel engaged by OLA , or the NC Attorney General’s Office are authorized to provide legal advice to the University. Minimum Requirements Bachelor’s degree in paralegal studies, legal studies, public administration, business administration, or a related discipline from an appropriately accredited institution, and three years of progressively responsible experience in a legal, compliance, or public sector administrative environment; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Bachelor’s degree in paralegal studies or legal studies, or a paralegal certificate from an ABA -approved or appropriately accredited program, and five years of progressively responsible experience in a legal, compliance, or public sector administrative environment. Preference will also be given to candidates with experience administering public records requests under a state public records statute; experience with contract administration, litigation support, or coordination with outside counsel; experience in a higher education or public sector legal office; and current certification through NALA , NFPA , or a comparable paralegal credentialing body. Required License or Certification Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. On-site (Employees are primarily in the office and/or have a critical job requirement that requires dedicated office space on-site) Position Information Working Title Legal Operations Manager Position Number 000172 Recruitment Salary Range commensurate with education and experience FLSA Exempt Appointment Type Permanent - Full-time Tenure Track No FTE 40 hours/week, 12 months If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Office of Legal Affairs Organizational Location Legal Affairs, Risk and Compliance Organizational Unit Office of Legal Affairs Posting Detail Information Posting Number EPA3192 Open Date 09/01/2026 Close Date - for postings that do not use Open Until Filled Open Until Filled Yes Open Until Filled Minimum Application Period Postings: Positions remaining posted after this date are continuing to accept applications, but may close at any time. Applications received by this date will receive full consideration, applications received after this date may receive consideration depending upon the status of the search Date Position Available 08/26/2026 Special Instructions to Applicant You must complete and submit an electronic application for employment to be considered. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must attach a DD 214 form. Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty with your application during the process of applying to the job posting. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. Employee Benefits available to NC A & T permanent employees include the following and more; Accrued Vacation and Sick Leave for Eligible Employees Community Service Leave Aetna – State Health Benefits of North Carolina NCFlex – Vision, Dental, Flexible Spending Account, Life Insurance and more 12 Paid Holidays Teachers and State Employees Retirement System ( TSERS ) Optional Supplemental Plans – 401k, 403b, 457b and 457 Employee Assistance Program ( EAP ) Campus Recreation Center Discount University Bookstore Discount and more This position may be eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41420 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
