mmuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title Update Classification Type SHRA Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: Minimum Experience/Education Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Minimum: High school diploma/ GED Preferred: Prefer 1-2 years of experience in security, parking, or related field. Prefer a candidate with T2 or other software experience. Required License or Certification Valid NC Driver’s License Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The purpose of the Enforcement Officer position is to routinely patrol campus using a vehicle equipped with mobile License Plate Recognition to ensure compliance with all State, Federal, and University policies and laws regarding parking. Candidates should have a good understanding of Microsoft Outlook, radio protocol, customer service best practices, and should be comfortable with learning new technology and software. This position may require occasional weekend or evening work. Primary Function of Organizational Unit Parking and Transportation Services provides transit options to students, faculty, staff and visitors, issues permits to allow lawful parking on the University’s campus, issue citations to motorists in violation of University policies, and maintain University parking and transit infrastructure. Work Hours 8am-5pm, M-F. Occasional weekend or evening work may be required to assist with campus events. Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Position Information Working Title Temporary Parking Enforcement Officer/ Property Security Officer Competency Level Contributing Position Number Recruitment Range $20/hour FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Full-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Campus Enterprises O