    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41549": {
      "title": "Temporary Research and Lab Tech (Various Disciplines)",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary Research and Lab Tech (Various Disciplines) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary Research and Lab Tech (Various Disciplines) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title Classification Type Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: Minimum Experience/Education Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or equivalency; or a combination of education and experience Basic computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office applications (Word, Excel, Outlook). Preferred Qualifications: Coursework or degree in a science, technology, engineering, mathematics ( STEM ), social science, health science, or related field. Previous experience in a laboratory, research, academic, or data collection environment. Experience entering, organizing, or analyzing data. Familiarity with laboratory safety procedures and practices. Experience working in a higher education, healthcare, or research setting. Required License or Certification N/A Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position Position Purpose North Carolina A&T State University periodically has temporary staffing needs to support research activities and laboratory operations across the University. This recruitment is intended to identify qualified candidates for temporary Research Assistant and Laboratory Technician opportunities as workforce needs arise. Temporary assignments may be available in a variety of academic, scientific, engineering, agricultural, health, and social science research environments. Opportunities may support faculty-led research projects, grant-funded initiatives, laboratory operations, data collection efforts, field studies, and other research-related activities. Assignment length, work schedule, and level of responsibility will vary based on departmental and project needs. Potential Duties and Responsibilities Duties may include, but are not limited to: Assisting faculty, staff, and research personnel with ongoing research projects and laboratory activities Collecting, recording, organizing, and maintaining research data and documentation Conducting routine laboratory procedures and experiments in accordance with established protocols Preparing laboratory materials, equipment, specimens, and supplies for research activities Operating, cleaning, calibrating, and maintaining laboratory equipment and instruments Assisting with data entry, analysis, and preparation of reports, presentations, and research summaries Supporting fieldwork activities, surveys, interviews, and other research-related data collection efforts Maintaining accurate records and ensuring compliance with laboratory safety standards and research protocols Managing inventory of laboratory supplies and assisting with procurement activities as needed Assisting with literature reviews, research documentation, and administrative support functions Supporting the implementation of grant-funded research projects and special initiatives Performing other duties as assigned by the supervisor or principal investigator Additional Information Specific job duties, qualifications, work schedules, and assignment durations will vary depending on the needs of the hiring department and the nature of the temporary assignment. Details regarding individual opportunities will be discussed with candidates selected for an interview. Only applicants who meet the minimum qualifications for a temporary opportunity will be considered. To enhance consideration, applicants are encouraged to upload all relevant certifications, licenses, training records, and other professional credentials at the time of application. Please Note: This posting will remain active for six (6) months. Applicants who wish to be considered for temporary opportunities after the posting has expired must submit a new application to the subsequent posting. Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina A&T State University is one of the nation’s leading land-grant institutions, distinguished by its commitment to excellence in teaching, research, public service, and community engagement. As the largest historically Black college and university ( HBCU ) in the United States and a doctoral, high research activity institution, the University fosters innovation through interdisciplinary research, creative scholarship, and transformative educational experiences. A constituent institution of the University of North Carolina System , North Carolina A&T offers a comprehensive range of undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral degree programs designed to prepare students for leadership and success in a global society. The University serves approximately 12,000 students and employs nearly 2,000 faculty and staff dedicated to advancing knowledge, promoting economic development, and addressing the needs of local, national, and global communities. Through its mission of exemplary instruction, scholarly and creative research, and meaningful public service, North Carolina A&T continues to expand its impact as a premier public, land-grant research university. Work Hours Various; Based on departmental need Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Position Information Working Title Temporary Research and Lab Tech (Various Disciplines) Competency Level Contributing Position Number Recruitment Range Commensurate with education and experience FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Full-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Staffing Services Organizational Location Human Resources Organizational Unit Temporary Employment Posting Detail Information Posting Number SHRA3264 Open Date 09/01/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Special Instructions to Applicant To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41548 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate where you learned about this employment opportunity: North Carolina A&T State University employment web page University of North Carolina System employment web page Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Education Research Consortium (HERC) Indeed.com Listserv Other * How many years of experience do you have as a Laboratory Research Technician? None 1 - 2 years 2 - 3 years 3 - 4 years 5 years or more * Please describe your research/laboratory experience. (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Cover Letter Other Document Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
