    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41668": {
      "title": "Temporary Pool - Shuttle Driver",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary Pool - Shuttle Driver Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary Pool - Shuttle Driver Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title Update Classification Type SHRA Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: Minimum Experience/Education Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Minimum: Valid unrestricted CDL license with Passenger Endorsement Two years of relative experience Demonstrated possession of the competencies necessary to perform the work. Preferred: High School Diploma or equivalent 5 Years of Experience. Required License or Certification CDL license with Passenger Endorsement Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position The primary purpose of this position is to provide safe, dependable, and customer-focused transportation services for students, faculty, staff, and visitors through the operation of university-owned shuttle buses, vans, and other assigned vehicles. The Shuttle Driver/Vehicle Equipment Operator is responsible for transporting passengers to designated destinations, adhering to established routes and schedules, conducting routine vehicle safety inspections, and ensuring compliance with all applicable traffic laws and university policies. Through professional, courteous, and service-oriented interactions, this position contributes to a positive campus experience while supporting the efficiency, accessibility, and overall success of the University’s transportation operations. A strong commitment to safety, reliability, and exceptional customer service is essential to the role Important Notice: Specific job duties, qualifications, work schedules, and assignment durations will vary depending on the needs of the hiring department and the nature of the temporary assignment. Details will be discussed with candidates selected for an interview. Only applicants who meet the minimum qualifications for a temporary opportunity will be considered. To enhance consideration, applicants are encouraged to upload all relevant certifications, licenses, training records, and other professional credentials at the time of application. Please Note: This posting will remain active for six (6) months. Applicants who wish to be considered for temporary opportunities after the posting has expired must submit a new application to the subsequent posting. Primary Function of Organizational Unit NC A&T’s Parking & Transportation Services is dedicated to providing safe, efficient, and accessible campus transportation solutions that support the University’s mission and enhance the campus experience for students, faculty, staff, visitors, and guests. The department manages parking and transportation resources to ensure convenient campus access while promoting a welcoming, orderly, and secure environment. Through the consistent enforcement of parking rules and regulations, Parking & Transportation Services helps maintain the safe and effective use of university facilities and infrastructure. As a customer-focused organization, the department is committed to delivering responsive, professional, and service-oriented support, striving to provide exceptional service and positive experiences for all members of the campus community. Work Hours Operation Hours are Monday through Friday 7:00 A.M. until 2:00 A.M.  Services are also provided on weekends, and special events. Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Position Information Working Title Temporary Pool - Shuttle Driver Competency Level Contributing Position Number Recruitment Range Commensurate with education and experience FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Full-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Talent Solutions Organizational Location Human Resources Organizational Unit Temporary Employment Posting Detail Information Posting Number SHRA3275 Open Date 09/23/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Special Instructions to Applicant To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41106 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a valid commercial driving license with passenger endorsement? Yes No * How many years of Commercial Driving experience do you have? Less than 2 years More the 2 years More than 5 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Cover Letter Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Copy of Education Transcripts Other Document Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
