    "https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41552": {
      "title": "Temporary Administrative Support Professional",
      "description": "NCAT Applicant Portal | Temporary Administrative Support Professional Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs NOTIFY ME ABOUT N.C. A&T JOBS Log In /Create Account Help N.C. A&T Applicant FAQ's Current N.C. A&T Employee Log in Please use this link to log into AggieTalent using the SSO Authentication link. This will log you into the Main Departmental Portal. Scroll down to “My Links” and select Apply Now. This important step will log you into your Application Account that is now tied to your Employee Account. N.C. A&T Temporary Employees will need to use the Log In/Create Account option listed above. Temporary Employment Student Employment Temporary Administrative Support Professional Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran's Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Posting Details Classification Information Position/Classification Title Classification Type Position required to work during periods of adverse weather or other emergencies: Minimum Experience/Education Preferred Years Experience, Skills, Training, Education Minimum Experience/Education High school diploma or equivalency and one (1) year of administrative, clerical, customer service, or office support experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience providing customer service and administrative support in a professional office environment. Basic computer skills and proficiency with common office software and technology. Preferred Experience/Education Associate’s degree in Business Administration, Office Administration, Public Administration, or a related field. Two (2) or more years of progressively responsible administrative or office support experience. Experience working in a higher education, government, or nonprofit environment. Experience scheduling meetings, managing calendars, coordinating events, or supporting projects. Experience with records management, data entry, report preparation, and maintaining confidential information. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and enterprise systems such as Banner, PeopleSoft, Workday, or similar administrative platforms. Demonstrated ability to prioritize multiple assignments and meet deadlines with minimal supervision. Required License or Certification N/A Position Overview Primary Purpose of Position Position Purpose North Carolina A&T State University periodically has temporary staffing needs to support administrative operations across campus. This recruitment is intended to identify qualified candidates for temporary Administrative Support opportunities as workforce needs arise. Temporary assignments may be available in a variety of offices and departments throughout the University. Opportunities may include providing clerical, customer service, office administration, coordination, records management, executive assistance, and operational support to faculty, staff, students, and campus visitors. Assignment length, work schedule, and level of responsibility will vary based on departmental needs. Potential Duties and Responsibilities Duties may include, but are not limited to: Providing general administrative and clerical support to departmental staff and/or leadership Greeting and assisting students, faculty, staff, and visitors in person, by phone, and through email correspondence Answering and directing telephone calls and responding to routine inquiries Preparing, proofreading, filing, scanning, and maintaining office documents and records Entering, updating, and maintaining information in databases, spreadsheets, and other electronic systems Scheduling appointments, meetings, and events, and coordinating related logistics Assisting with the preparation of reports, presentations, correspondence, and other business documents Monitoring and maintaining office supplies and assisting with procurement requests Supporting departmental projects, programs, and special initiatives Assisting with data collection, recordkeeping, and compliance-related documentation Maintaining confidential and sensitive information in accordance with University policies Performing other duties as assigned by the supervisor Additional Information Specific job duties, qualifications, work schedules, and assignment durations will vary depending on the needs of the hiring department and the nature of the temporary assignment. Details regarding individual opportunities will be discussed with candidates selected for an interview. Only applicants who meet the minimum qualifications for a temporary opportunity will be considered. To enhance consideration, applicants are encouraged to upload all relevant certifications, licenses, training records, and other professional credentials at the time of application. Please Note: This posting will remain active for six (6) months. Applicants who wish to be considered for temporary opportunities after the posting has expired must submit a new application to the subsequent posting. Primary Function of Organizational Unit North Carolina A&T State University is a nationally recognized 1890 land-grant doctoral research institution with a distinguished legacy of excellence in teaching, research, innovation, and community engagement. As the largest historically Black college and university ( HBCU ) in the United States, the University serves more than 13,000 students and employs over 2,000 faculty and staff. A constituent institution of the University of North Carolina ( UNC ) System, North Carolina A&T offers more than 90 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral degree programs through eight academic colleges. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges ( SACSCOC ) and is committed to providing a learner-centered environment that fosters academic excellence, interdisciplinary scholarship, and impactful research. Through its strategic vision, North Carolina A&T advances discovery, creativity, and innovation while preparing graduates to become leaders in a global society. The University’s commitment to excellence in education, research, and public service continues to drive its influence and impact at the state, national, and international levels. Work Hours Hours and days may vary; schedule will be determined based upon business need of the hiring department. Is this position eligible for a remote or hybrid work arrangement, consistent with university and state policies. Key Responsibilities and Related Competencies Position Information Working Title Temporary Administrative Support Professional Competency Level Contributing Position Number Recruitment Range Commensurate with experience FLSA Non-Exempt Appointment Type Temporary - Full-time FTE If Time Limited,  Appointment Length Organizational Division Staffing Services Organizational Location Human Resources Organizational Unit Temporary Employment Posting Detail Information Posting Number SHRA3265 Open Date 09/01/2026 Close Date 02/28/2027 Special Instructions to Applicant To be considered for employment, an electronic application must be completed and submitted. Resumes will not be accepted in lieu of completing an electronic application. Applicants seeking Veteran’s Preference must upload a DD 214 Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty to their application during the application process. Final candidates are subject to criminal and sex offender background checks. North Carolina A&T State University participates in E-Verify to confirm work authorization in the United States. Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. North Carolina A&T State University is an Equal Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer. No one who applies or seeks employment will be denied admission to or employment at North Carolina A&T State University on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, veteran status, political affiliation, genetic information or sexual orientation and sexual identity. N.C. A&T employees are generally required to reside in North Carolina, within a 2-hour commuting distance of their assigned duty station. Quick Link https://jobs.ncat.edu/postings/41550 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please describe your proficiencies with various computer technology systems and software programs such as Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Banner, AggieMart, and any other technology systems. (Open Ended Question) * How many years of experience do you have in office administration? 1-2 3-5 5-7 More than 7 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Certificate of Release or Discharge from Active Duty (DD-214) Copy of Education Transcripts Other Document Contact Division of Human Resources Phone: (336) 334-7862 Fax: (336) 285-2799 Email: hr@ncat.edu 1806 E. Market Street, Suite 401, Greensboro, NC 27401 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
